1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
What if a city suddenly began dancing

2
00:00:02,510 --> 00:00:04,160
and could not stop?

3
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:08,060
In Strasbourg, in the summer of 1518,

4
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:11,140
one exhausted woman began to move in

5
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:13,800
the street. Then another joined her.

6
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,780
Soon, the city was watching a frightening

7
00:00:16,790 --> 00:00:18,460
outbreak no one understood.

8
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:20,960
The dancers multiplied.

9
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:23,040
Some moved for hours,

10
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:24,080
some for days,

11
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:27,680
while horrified neighbors watched their strength disappear.

12
00:00:27,690 --> 00:00:31,600
The exact numbers remain uncertain but the

13
00:00:31,610 --> 00:00:34,320
terror they left behind became notorious.

14
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:37,860
The authorities searched for a cure and

15
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:39,300
made a desperate decision:

16
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:41,260
give the dancers room,

17
00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:43,000
and bring in musicians.

18
00:00:43,740 --> 00:00:46,340
They believed movement might burn the sickness

19
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:50,520
out. Instead, the remedy risked feeding the

20
00:00:50,530 --> 00:00:51,020
spectacle.

21
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:54,080
But the music could not hide the

22
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:58,640
cost. Chroniclers described bodies driven past exhaustion

23
00:00:58,650 --> 00:01:01,200
and people collapsing in the streets.

24
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:04,160
Later retellings speak of mass deaths,

25
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:07,640
though the surviving evidence cannot firmly prove

26
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:08,607
those numbers.

27
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:13,340
Centuries later, the mystery still resists a

28
00:01:13,350 --> 00:01:17,240
single answer. Historians have considered famine and

29
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:19,580
stress, belief, disease,

30
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:23,560
and social contagion but no surviving evidence

31
00:01:23,570 --> 00:01:25,861
proves one cause beyond doubt.

32
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:29,520
What remains is more disturbing than a

33
00:01:29,530 --> 00:01:33,200
ghost story: a real city confronting behavior

34
00:01:33,210 --> 00:01:34,640
it could not control,

35
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:38,120
while its leaders acted without understanding what

36
00:01:38,130 --> 00:01:38,860
they were seeing.

37
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:41,580
The strangest part was not that people

38
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:44,580
danced. It was that everyone around them

39
00:01:44,590 --> 00:01:45,917
watched and joined in.
